                ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\n\t\\left[\n\t\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{array}\n\t\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y &=-5 \\\\ y &=-10,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$"
